<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joseph Dudley</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1647–<a href="/years/1720">1720</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joseph Dudley was a Massachusetts-born colonial official, son of Governor Thomas Dudley. After the Massachusetts charter was revoked, he headed the interim government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> from 1686 until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edmund-andros">Edmund Andros</a> arrived. Jailed after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a> revolt of 1689, he later returned as royal governor of the Province of Massachusetts Bay from 1702 to 1715.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joseph-dudley.jpg" alt="Joseph Dudley" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Peter Lely · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joseph_Dudley_attributed_to_Peter_Lely.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
